desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Detect Tensorflow"
	title_zh: "Detect Tensorflow"
	type: maintainability
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-maintainability-detect-tensorflow"
	risk: "Maintainability"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `detect-tensorflow` (ai/python/detect-tensorflow.yaml).
Original message: Possibly found usage of AI tooling: Tensorflow
References:
- https://semgrep.dev/blog/2024/detecting-shadow-ai
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.py": <<<POS
import tensorflow
POS
	"safefile://pos.py": <<<NEG
import json
NEG
)

${*.py}.pattern_regex(/(?:import\s+tensorflow)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "Detect Tensorflow",
	title_zh: "Detect Tensorflow",
	message: "Detect Tensorflow detected.",
}
